course: dictionary
lesson: 12858
title: Engraved: carved, or fixed in memory
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Engraved means cut or carved into a hard surface, such as metal, stone, glass or wood. «Her name was engraved on the silver cup.» The cup is hard, and someone carved the letters into it so they stay there.
explain: Engraved can also mean fixed firmly in your memory. «The day is engraved on my mind.» Nobody is carving the day into your brain. It means you will remember that day for a long time.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in a word like carved or remembered. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right idea.
fact: Engrave is the verb. Engraved is its past form, and it can also be an adjective, as in «an engraved ring».
fact: «Engraved» means cut or carved into a hard surface such as metal, stone, glass or wood.
fact: «Engraved» can also mean fixed firmly in your memory, as in «engraved in his memory».
fact: An engraving is a picture printed from a cut metal plate, like some old pictures in history books.
fact: Engraved words are often found on trophies, rings, medals, gravestones and plaques.
exercise: «His name was engraved on the cup.» What does engraved mean here? | Painted in bright colours | Spoken out loud | *Cut or carved into the metal | Lost under the water
exercise: «The day is engraved on my mind.» What does engraved mean here? | Forgotten quickly | Drawn in pencil | *Fixed firmly in your memory | Printed on a box
exercise: Which word is another form of the verb engrave? | engine | enough | *engraves | engage
test: «The old bridge had dates engraved in its stone.» Where were the dates? | *Carved into the stone | Written in pencil on paper | Painted on the stone with a brush
test: An engraving in an old history book is a picture that was | Drawn by a child with crayons | Made of wood and glass | Sung as a song | *Printed from a cut metal plate
exam: «Her initials were engraved on the back of the gold medal, and she was proud of it.» What does engraved most likely mean here? | Lost in the race | *Carved into the metal | Whispered to a friend | Painted in bright colours
